course: dictionary
lesson: 9305
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. The word specimen is a good example.
explain: «Scientists describe thousands of new species every year, mostly insects, plants and small sea animals, and each one needs a scientific name, a type specimen kept in a museum and a scientific paper.» Here a specimen is one example of a plant or animal that is collected and studied. The clues are kept in a museum and scientific paper.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "A type example kept in a museum" still makes sense, so you have it right. A doctor's specimen is a different meaning, and the clue would be a doctor or a test.
fact: A specimen is one example of a plant, animal, rock or other thing that is collected and studied.
fact: In science lessons, specimens are collected, labelled, measured and looked at under a microscope.
fact: In health, a specimen is a small amount of blood or urine that a doctor tests.
fact: Museums keep specimens of fossils, insects and birds.
fact: Informally, a «fine specimen» is a joking way to describe a good or funny example of a person or animal.
exercise: «...a type specimen kept in a museum and a scientific paper.» In this sentence, what is a specimen? | A cup of tea | A loud noise made by a machine | *One example of a plant or animal that is collected and studied | A kind of sport played with a ball
exercise: A child puts a leaf into a specimen jar in science. What is the leaf? | *A specimen to be looked at and studied | A letter to send home | A toy for playtime | A drink for the class
exercise: Which word in «...a type specimen kept in a museum and a scientific paper» is the clue that the specimen is looked after? | scientific | *museum | insects | thousands
test: A doctor asks for a specimen of your blood. What does the doctor want? | A new pair of shoes | A drink of water | *A small sample to test | A map of the hospital
test: Your friend says, «Look at this fine specimen!» about a funny-looking dog. What does your friend mean? | A dog that is very ill | A dog that is lost | A dog's favourite toy | *A good or funny example of a dog
exam: In the sentence «Scientists describe thousands of new species every year...», what does specimen mean? | Pet rock | *One example of a plant or animal, kept and studied | Small machine | Lost property
